.\" Man page for YouNeeK Death Terminal. Keep in sync with `deathterminal --help`.
.TH DEATHTERMINAL 1 "2026-10-17" "YouNeeK Death Terminal 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
deathterminal \- brutalist GPU terminal emulator with AI suggestions, built\-in SSH and Lua plugins
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B deathterminal
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B deathterminal
.B \-\-ssh
.I target
.br
.B deathterminal
.B \-\-ssh\-session
.I target
.RB [ \-L | \-R | \-D
.IR spec ]...
.br
.B deathterminal
.B \-\-plugins
.RB list | enable
.IR name | \fBdisable\fP " " name
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B YouNeeK Death Terminal
is a terminal emulator written in Zig. It renders with Vulkan (with a software
fallback), shapes text with HarfBuzz, and supports tabs and split panes, an
xterm\-compatible VT core (including 80/132\-column switching), OSC 52/7/133,
an optional OpenAI\-compatible AI assistant, a built\-in SSH client
(libssh2) and sandboxed Lua plugins.
.PP
Without
.B \-\-gui
it runs headless in the current terminal (the grid is re\-drawn into the host
terminal), which is useful for testing and over SSH.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Use
.I file
(a
.B .lua
config, or a legacy
.B key = value
text file) instead of the default location.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-default\-config
Print a documented config.lua containing every default.
.TP
.B \-\-lua\-unsafe
Give config.lua the full Lua standard library (io, os.execute, require).
.TP
.BI \-\-print\-shell\-integration " bash|zsh|fish"
Print the OSC 133 shell\-integration snippet for the given shell.
.TP
.BI \-\-ssh " target"
Open a window connected over SSH.
.I target
is a
.B config.ssh.profiles
name, a
.I ~/.ssh/config
Host, or
.IR user @ host [: port ].
.TP
.BI \-\-ssh\-session " target"
Run the SSH client inside the current terminal; accepts
.BR \-L ", " \-R " and " \-D
forwards.
.TP
.BI \-\-ssh\-ctl " pid cmd"
Control a running SSH session:
.BR status ", " list ", " toggle " n, " on " n, " off " n, " add " spec, " reconnect .
.TP
.B \-\-plugins list\fR | \fBenable\fR \fIname\fR | \fBdisable\fR \fIname
Show installed plugins and their permissions, or switch one on or off.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-plugins
Start without loading any plugin.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-ai
Disable AI command suggestions.
.TP
.B \-\-headless
Run without a GUI window (the default).
.TP
.B \-\-gui
Open a native window (Wayland, X11, Win32 or Cocoa); falls back to headless.
.TP
.B \-\-share
Host this terminal and print the invite (LAN IP, port, and code). Stays up
until the shell exits. See
.IR docs/SHARING.md .
.TP
.BI \-\-join " invite"
Watch that shared pane. \fIinvite\fP is the code printed by
.B \-\-share
or a
.I deathterminal://join/
link.
.TP
.BI \-\-scale " n"
UI scale 1\(en4 (default: from DPI, compositor or environment).
.TP
.BI \-\-backend " name"
Window backend:
.BR auto ", " x11 ", " wayland ", " win32 ", " cocoa .
.TP
.BI \-\-font " retro|default"
Font renderer (retro is the built\-in 8x8 bitmap font).
.TP
.BI \-\-font\-family " name"
Font family (looked up with fontconfig on Linux, in the system font folders on
Windows and macOS). Default: the bundled JetBrains Mono.
.TP
.BI \-\-font\-size " pt"
Font size in points (default 11; Ctrl+= / Ctrl+\- / Ctrl+0 zoom).
.TP
.BI \-\-line\-height " n"
Cell height multiplier (default 1.0).
.PP
Command\-line flags override the config file.
.SH KEYS
The defaults below can be changed or disabled in config.lua
.RB ( config.keys ", " config.default_keybindings ).
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+C / Ctrl+Shift+V
Copy the selection / paste the clipboard (Shift+Insert pastes PRIMARY).
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+F
Search the scrollback.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+T / Ctrl+Shift+Alt+W
New tab / close tab.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+E / Ctrl+Shift+O / Ctrl+Shift+W
Split right / split down / close pane.
.TP
.B Alt+arrows / Alt+Shift+arrows
Move focus between panes / resize the focused pane.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+P
Command palette. On macOS this is
.BR Cmd+Shift+P .
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+S
SSH palette (profiles and forwards).
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+A
AI: explain and fix the last error.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+R
Reload the configuration.
.PP
On macOS the Command key stands in for Ctrl+Shift (Cmd+C, Cmd+V, Cmd+T, ...).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/death\-terminal/config.lua
User configuration (default
.IR ~/.config/death\-terminal/config.lua ).
On Windows:
.IR %APPDATA%\edeath\-terminal\econfig.lua .
Saving it reloads it live.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/death\-terminal/plugins/
Lua plugins, one directory each (manifest.lua, init.lua).
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/deathterminal/
README, CHANGELOG, configuration and plugin documentation, example config and
plugins.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SHELL
Shell to run when
.B config.shell.program
is empty (Windows: pwsh, then powershell, then %COMSPEC%).
.TP
.B DT_SCALE\fR, \fBGDK_SCALE\fR, \fBQT_SCALE_FACTOR
UI scale hints when no
.B \-\-scale
is given.
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY\fR, \fBDISPLAY
Select the Wayland or X11 backend.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of the shell (or SSH session) when it ends; 2 for usage errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xterm (1),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR ssh_config (5)
.PP
